# Type labels (Projects + Insights)

On `.projects-page`, `.project-detail`, `.insights-page`, `.insight-detail`:

1. **No fill** — no border, background, or capsule padding on type labels.
2. **Font** — `Test Pitch Sans` Semibold via `@font-face` → `/fonts/TestPitchSans-Semibold.otf` (same-origin; CDN alone lacks CORS for `@font-face`). CSS: `--font-type-label`.
3. **Size** — shared `--type-chip-font` (current size, −3% recipe). Same everywhere: featured, cards, Related, case hero tag.
4. **Color** — gray (`--type-label-color`, ~50% white).
5. **Title + description** in card/lead meta — **white** (`#fff`).
6. **Top-align with title** — every type label (and its chip list wrapper) uses `align-self: start` / `align-items: start`. Never baseline or vertical-center labels against titles.

Applies to `.project-type-chip`, `.insight-chip`, `.project-case-demo__tag`.

Filter involvement pills are separate UI — not this recipe.

# Featured lead meta only

**Scope:** `.project-featured__meta` and `.insights-lead__meta` only.

1. Label `max-content`, end-aligned, top-aligned.
2. Gaps total **13%** (`6.5%` + `6.5%`).
3. Title + description share remaining width equally.

Do **not** apply this gap formula to filter/Related cards or case-detail hero meta.

# Filter / Related cards

Title up to **65%** | type label end-aligned / top-aligned | description full width under. Label **size** still comes from the unified tokens above.

# Project detail hero meta (mobile ≤800px)

`.project-case-demo__hero-copy` matches the card stack (not featured-lead 13% gaps):

1. Title ≤ **60%** | type label **end-aligned / top-aligned** (gap between).
2. Description on the next row, **full** usable width, left-aligned.
